## 2. CSS Design Tokens

All sizing uses CSS custom properties defined in `globals.css`. These tokens
scale fluidly via `clamp()` and lock to spacious values on touch devices.

**NEVER hardcode pixel sizes like `text-[11px]` or `w-6 h-6`.** Always use the
token-based classes or the CSS variables.

### How to use tokens in Tailwind

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — uses tokens, auto-adapts
<button className="text-body min-h-touch px-card">Save</button>
<p className="text-sub">Subtitle</p>
<span className="text-label">LABEL</span>

// ❌ BAD — hardcoded, too small on mobile
<button className="text-[11px] px-2 py-1.5">Save</button>
```

### Token reference

| Token | Range (min→max) | Touch lock | Tailwind class |
|-------|----------------|------------|----------------|
| `--text-body` | 14px → 16px | 16px | `text-body` |
| `--text-sub` | 12px → 14px | 14px | `text-sub` |
| `--text-label` | 10px → 12px | 12px | `text-label` |
| `--text-button` | 12px → 14px | 14px | `text-button` |
| `--text-heading` | 18px → 20px | 20px | `text-heading` |
| `--text-subheading` | 14px → 16px | 16px | `text-subheading` |
| `--size-touch` | 32px → 44px | 44px | `min-h-touch` / `min-w-touch` |
| `--size-touch-lg` | 36px → 48px | 48px | `min-h-touch-lg` |
| `--size-icon-btn` | 28px → 40px | 40px | `w-icon-btn h-icon-btn` |
| `--size-icon-sm` | 14px → 18px | 18px | `w-icon-sm h-icon-sm` |
| `--size-icon-md` | 16px → 20px | 20px | `w-icon-md h-icon-md` |
| `--size-icon-lg` | 20px → 24px | 24px | `w-icon-lg h-icon-lg` |
| `--space-card` | 12px → 16px | 16px | `px-card` / `py-card` |
| `--space-card-sm` | 8px → 12px | 12px | `px-card-sm` / `py-card-sm` |
| `--space-section` | 16px → 24px | 24px | `gap-section` / `mb-section` |
| `--size-input` | 36px → 48px | 48px | `h-input` |
| `--size-list-item` | 36px → 48px | 48px | `min-h-list-item` |

