## 3. Container Queries

### How container queries work

The `<main>` element in `DashboardShell` has `container-type: inline-size`.
All child components can use `@sm:`, `@md:`, `@lg:`, `@xl:` variants which
respond to the **main area's width**, not the viewport.

### Tailwind v4 container breakpoint values

These are NOT viewport breakpoints — they are smaller:

| Variant | Min container width |
|---------|---------------------|
| `@sm` | 384px (24rem) |
| `@md` | 448px (28rem) |
| `@lg` | 512px (32rem) |
| `@xl` | 576px (36rem) |

For component-level containers (Kanban columns, calendar cells, panels), add
`style={{ containerType: "inline-size" }}` to the wrapper element.

### Adding a container context

```tsx
// Make an element a size container
<div style={{ containerType: "inline-size" }}>
  {/* Children can now use @sm:, @md:, etc. based on THIS element's width */}
</div>
```

### The `cq-adapt` class

Add `cq-adapt` to any component that should have its typography, icons,
and spacing adapt based on the container's width. Touch targets (buttons,
inputs, list items) are NEVER reduced — they stay at the `pointer: coarse`
floor on touch devices.

- `≤320px` → compact (smaller text, tighter spacing)
- `321px–599px` → normal (balanced)
- `≥600px` → spacious (full mobile sizes)

```tsx
// Card that auto-adapts text and spacing, touch targets stay safe
<div className="cq-adapt rounded-xl border bg-card p-card">
  <h3 className="text-subheading font-semibold">Title</h3>
  <button className="min-h-touch text-button">Action</button>
</div>
```

### Existing container contexts

| Element | File | What it contains |
|---------|------|-----------------|
| `<main>` | `dashboard-shell.tsx` | All page content |
| Kanban column | `project-detail-client.tsx` | Task cards |
| Deal column | `deals-client.tsx` | Deal cards |
| Activity panel | `activity-panel.tsx` | Activity feed |
| Date panel | `publish-client.tsx` | Scheduled items |

